From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 07:01:49 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] PROTOTYPE pco: don't back-propagate loads into shared
 registers

Local experiment for amazon-suez, never to be sent (Imagination declines
LLM-generated code in src/imagination).

With PCO_DEBUG=preamble, zink's vertex preambles load uniforms straight
into the shared registers (back-propagation folds 'ld r; mov sh, r' into
'ld sh'), and every such vertex shader draws nothing on GX6250. The
working preambles (fragment, and vk-sample's vertex) load into temps and
copy. Keep loads, atomics and samples writing temps.

Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/imagination/pco/pco_opt.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/imagination/pco/pco_opt.c b/src/imagination/pco/pco_opt.c
index b9aedeae197..58bd41b4270 100644
--- a/src/imagination/pco/pco_opt.c
+++ b/src/imagination/pco/pco_opt.c
@@ -261,6 +261,19 @@ static inline bool try_back_prop_instr(struct pco_use *uses, pco_instr *instr)
    if (pco_ref_is_idx_reg(*pdest_from))
       return false;
 
+   /* PROTOTYPE: a vertex preamble whose loads wrote straight into shared
+    * registers ("ld sh0, ...") left them unwritten on GX6250: every vertex
+    * shader with such a preamble drew nothing. Keep memory operations
+    * writing temporaries and copy into the shared registers.
+    */
+   if (pco_ref_is_reg(*pdest_from) &&
+       pco_ref_get_reg_class(*pdest_from) == PCO_REG_CLASS_SHARED &&
+       (instr->op == PCO_OP_LD || instr->op == PCO_OP_LD_REGBL ||
+        instr->op == PCO_OP_ATOMIC || instr->op == PCO_OP_SMP ||
+        instr->op == PCO_OP_SMP_WRT)) {
+      return false;
+   }
+
    if (pco_ref_is_reg(*pdest_from) &&
        pco_ref_get_reg_class(*pdest_from) == PCO_REG_CLASS_PIXOUT) {
       return false;
